From 08a8a539cc1193e265b6a1201227f1232ac89f9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:44:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: the 68k template JIT (J2, first stage)

Hot loops' CodeBlocks are compiled by copying, for each bytecode
instruction, the 68k interpreter's own handler for it as a template
(offlineasm-py/m68k_templates.py) and writing the instruction's operands
into the copy (llint/M68KTemplateJIT.cpp). The copies fall through into
each other while PC moves on by one instruction, without the interpreter's
dispatch and operand decoding.

The code runs on the interpreter's frames, registers and register file, so
the two hand over at any instruction: op_loop_hint's tier-up (loop_osr)
jumps into the code, and the code leaves through jsc_m68k_tjit_redispatch
whenever PC moves anywhere else (a jump, a slow path that changed PC, an
exception), carrying on in the code if the CodeBlock has some at the new
PC, else in the interpreter.

Off by default: JSC_useM68KTemplateJIT=1 turns it on.
m68kTemplateJITMaximumBytecodeSize (4096) caps the CodeBlocks it compiles.
---
